(7114820, 1085623, 129807, '<td valign="top">(voted earlier, coming back to comment)<br/>My team and I were marveling at the dearth of comments in this challenge so I thought I would at least attempt to correct that a little:<br/>Sunset colours are magical and you have captured some of that here. You have used composition that leads the eye straight to the sun then allows the viewer to discover what lies on the horizon. However I feel that the foreground doesn''t quite work; the colours seem hinky (yes, it''s a word... it''s my word) and it seems out of focus with a strange black triangle image left along the edge. Perhaps a different element of foreground interest could have been included.</td>', '(voted earlier, coming back to comment)My team and I were marveling at the dearth of comments in this challenge so I thought I would at least attempt to correct that a little:Sunset colours are magical and you have captured some of that here. You have used composition that leads the eye straight to the sun then allows the viewer to discover what lies on the horizon. However I feel that the foreground doesn''t quite work; the colours seem hinky (yes, it''s a word... it''s my word) and it seems out of focus with a strange black triangle image left along the edge. Perhaps a different element of foreground interest could have been included.', '2013-10-12 08:22:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7114821, 1085577, 129807, '<td valign="top">(voted earlier, coming back to comment)<br/>My team and I were marveling at the dearth of comments in this challenge so I thought I would at least attempt to correct that a little:<br/>I really like this portrait as it speaks to the viewer regardless of whether you read the title or not. However, the pole behind his head is distracting; perhaps a crop just above his hat would help remove that focus while leaving more than enough environmental elements to still tell the story.</td>', '(voted earlier, coming back to comment)My team and I were marveling at the dearth of comments in this challenge so I thought I would at least attempt to correct that a little:I really like this portrait as it speaks to the viewer regardless of whether you read the title or not. However, the pole behind his head is distracting; perhaps a crop just above his hat would help remove that focus while leaving more than enough environmental elements to still tell the story.', '2013-10-12 08:28:01.000000', NULL, 1),
