(7115856, 1084990, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave this a 7. It has an artless feel to it similar to <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=76335" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bvy</a>, but with intriguing juxtapositions nonetheless. </i></td></tr></table> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=76335" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bvy</a>? I''m honored. It is indeed a hip shot.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pamb:</b></div><hr/><i> (voted earlier, coming back to comment) <br/>My team and I were marveling at the dearth of comments in this challenge so I thought I would at least attempt to correct that a little: <br/> <br/>What I like: the spots of colour are very well balanced.<br/>What I don''t necessarily like but understand you can''t help these things: <b>he</b>''s facing the ''wrong'' way. However, the colour keeps you in the frame anyway, so maybe it''s not that bad after all!<br/>I actually read the poster - interesting advertisement! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Bless you for the initiative. Just wanted to add that this is a woman in front, and that this fact is a hint to why I chose it for the challenge.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I gave this a 7. It has an artless feel to it similar to  bvy, but with intriguing juxtapositions nonetheless.   bvy? I''m honored. It is indeed a hip shot. Originally posted by pamb: (voted earlier, coming back to comment) My team and I were marveling at the dearth of comments in this challenge so I thought I would at least attempt to correct that a little:  What I like: the spots of colour are very well balanced.What I don''t necessarily like but understand you can''t help these things: he''s facing the ''wrong'' way. However, the colour keeps you in the frame anyway, so maybe it''s not that bad after all!I actually read the poster - interesting advertisement!  Bless you for the initiative. Just wanted to add that this is a woman in front, and that this fact is a hint to why I chose it for the challenge.', '2013-10-15 02:59:54.000000', NULL, 0),
